  "task": {
    "objective": "Construct traversable patterned paths and physically reach and commission a socket. Private destination preferences and shared claim bonuses shape which paths actors favor.",
    "natural_termination": "Every builder has commissioned one socket; no puzzle solver or construction score decides completion.",
    "interaction": "Every placed tile imposes equality constraints on neighboring edge bits. Rotation consumes pins and can change a peer's next placement mask or movement route. Inventory is finite, placements permanent, handoffs preserve tile identity and orientation.",
